+### [Cone Scatter Initialization](21774-cone-scatter-initialization.md)
+Cone Scatter Initialization (CSI) is a technique for 3D Gaussian Splatting that enriches sparse point clouds (typically from COLMAP) by scattering new points within a predefined viewing frustum, specifically to address depth coverage issues in low-light or nighttime scenes where COLMAP fails to produce high-quality distant points. Unlike standard initialization which relies solely on existing sparse matches, CSI ensures Gaussians form at correct, deeper depths, preventing the generation of structures at incorrect depths and lack of fine details.
 
 ### Neural Point Cloud Initialization from COLMAP
-A method to initialize the neural point cloud and their features for Point-NeRF using an external point cloud reconstruction (specifically COLMAP) [S10]. It solves the problem of how to provide initial positions, variances, and feature vectors for the neural points [S10]. The variance parameter $\gamma_i$ for each point $p_i$ is initialized to 0.3 [S10]. To acquire the feature vector $f_i$ for a point $p_i$, views where the point is occluded are ruled out, and the view closest to the point is selected [S10].
+A method to initialize the neural point cloud and their features for Point-NeRF using an external point cloud reconstruction (specifically COLMAP). It solves the problem of how to provide initial positions, variances, and feature vectors for the neural points. The variance parameter $\gamma_i$ for each point $p_i$ is initialized to 0.3. To acquire the feature vector $f_i$ for a point $p_i$, views where the point is occluded are ruled out, and the view where the camera is closest to the point is selected. The point is unprojected onto the feature maps extracted by the Image Feature Extraction 2D CNN (Gf) from the selected closest view to obtain $f_i$. During optimization, the confidence score of valid points is pushed to 1 [S10].
 
 ### Binary Gaussian Hierarchy Construction
-The hierarchy is a binary tree [S11, unofficial]. Leaf nodes contain the full set of optimized Gaussian properties (base color, SH coefficients, position, covariance) [S11, unofficial]. Internal nodes store merged approximations of their two child nodes [S11, unofficial].
